aqueousThermo
{
source "hfAq [kJ/mol] -518.37: dHf(aq glycine) -514.36 - dH_ion1 +4.01 -- Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049, Table 3, p. 1054, and Table 6, p. 1057 (read from a page image), the aqueous glycine is dHf(cr) -528.52 +/- 0.50 plus dH(soln) +14.16 ## sAq [J/mol/K] 189.95: S(aq glycine) 158.45 - dS_ion1 (-31.5) -- Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049, Table 3, p. 1054, and Table 6, p. 1057 (read from a page image)";
hfAq { value -518370; unit J/mol;}
